{"decision":"edit","issues":[{"quote":"a figure wrapped in a fibrous tan-and-green ghillie suit lowers its head toward the stock.","problem":"Invented action. Across all frames the figure's head is obscured by the ghillie camouflage and never visibly moves toward the stock; this also contradicts the later claim that the figure is motionless."},{"quote":"the overall composition holds steady from the first sample to the last.","problem":"Annotation phrase 'sample' should not appear in a direct video description."},{"quote":"the rifle, bipod, and camouflage keeping the same positions relative to the frame edges.","problem":"Overly absolute; the caption itself notes minor handheld camera instability, so the positions drift slightly rather than staying exactly the same relative to the edges."},{"quote":"The excerpt ends without any change to the held position or any resolution of the wait.","problem":"Annotation phrase 'excerpt' should not appear in a direct video description."}],"caption":"The video captures a close, low-angle view of a scoped rifle resting on a bipod amid tall grass and brush. The barrel sits in the foreground, blurred and pointing toward the camera, while the optical scope stays sharp in the mid-frame. Behind it, a figure wrapped in a fibrous tan-and-green ghillie suit holds position, its head obscured by the camouflage.

The dense vegetation fills the frame with no clear horizon, and the overall composition holds steady throughout. Only very subtle variation appears, consistent with a slight sway of foreground grass blades and minor handheld camera instability. The shooter's posture behind the scope does not change appreciably, the rifle, bipod, and camouflage remaining essentially fixed relative to the frame edges.

No recoil, muzzle flash, bolt cycling, or barrel displacement is visible, so no shot occurs. The aiming state simply persists, the figure motionless behind the optic, ending without any change to the held position or any resolution of the wait.","length_note":""}
